      "text": "Dual-threat quarterback\nHistorically , dual threat quarterbacks in the National Football League ( NFL ) were uncommon , with Michael Vick being considered a rarity in the early 2000s . In recent years , quarterbacks with dual-threat capabilities have become more popular . Current NFL quarterbacks considered to be dual-threat include Cam Newton , Russell Wilson , Colin Kaepernick , and Tyrod Taylor ."
